# One rule, no exceptions: the repository is UTF-8 and the working tree is
# ISO8859-1, so a checkout on z/OS is tagged ASCII, which is what make, sh,
# awk and the compiler need when they read it through the EBCDIC converter.
# This is the same line the zopen community's git port uses.  Everything in
# the tree stays 7-bit; a box character belongs on the terminal, not in the
# source.
* text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=ISO8859-1
